# evidence-for: US-007, AC-030, FR-023
#
# AC-030. A page whose title lives in frontmatter, with no description and no
# `# ` heading, gets its first prose line as the summary. The header above it is
# the sixth source: the checkout's directory name, published as the filesystem
# spells it. It is the one header source that does not run through one_line, and
# the comment above the chain now says so rather than claiming every source is
# cleaned -- `# {app}` is what that costs.
#
# FR-023. The two suppressors on the README route, each measured on a README
# carrying only the one it exercises: the stub marker with no brace, and the
# brace with no marker. Each drops the README's line and leaves the header with
# no `> ` summary rather than publishing a skeleton. They shared one fixture
# until this cycle, which is how the marker check came to be covered by nothing.
